    answer: '<p>Check for updates at least <strong>monthly</strong>, or enable automatic updates if available:</p><ul><li><strong>Security patches:</strong> Fix newly discovered vulnerabilities</li><li><strong>Bug fixes:</strong> Improve stability and performance</li><li><strong>New features:</strong> Sometimes add WPA3 or other improvements</li></ul><p>Set a monthly reminder to check, or use a router with automatic updates (ASUS, eero, Google Nest).</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Is my ISP-provided router secure enough?',
    answer: '<p>ISP routers are often <strong>adequate but not optimal</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Maintained by ISP, automatic updates, support included</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> Often older hardware, limited features, may have ISP backdoors</li></ul><p>For serious remote work, consider upgrading to a quality third-party router (ASUS, Netgear, TP-Link) for better security features and performance.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should I use WPA3 or WPA2?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Use WPA3 if all your devices support it.</strong> Otherwise:</p><ul><li><strong>WPA3:</strong> Latest standard, best security, may not work with older devices</li><li><strong>WPA2-Personal (AES):</strong> Still secure, broadly compatible</li><li><strong>WPA2/WPA3 Transitional:</strong> Best of both worlds—WPA3 for capable devices, WPA2 fallback for older ones</li></ul><p>Never use WEP or WPA (without the "2" or "3")—they\'re broken.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need a separate network for smart home devices?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Yes, ideally.</strong> Smart devices often have poor security:</p><ul><li>Many never receive security updates</li><li>Can be entry points for attackers</li><li>Some send data to unknown servers</li></ul><p>Put IoT devices on a guest network or VLAN, separate from your work devices. This way, a compromised smart bulb can\'t access your work laptop.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'What\'s the best router for security?',
    answer: '<p>Look for routers with:</p><ul><li><strong>Regular firmware updates:</strong> ASUS, Netgear, TP-Link are generally good</li><li><strong>WPA3 support:</strong> Current standard</li><li><strong>VLAN support:</strong> For network segmentation</li><li><strong>Built-in VPN server:</strong> For remote access</li></ul><p>Specific recommendations: ASUS RT-AX86U, Netgear Nighthawk, TP-Link Archer series. For mesh: eero Pro, ASUS ZenWiFi, Google Nest WiFi Pro.</p>'
